%% SECTION Calculations Workout
@@ | fill
BAC = $120,000. The project is planned to take 12 months at an even rate. After 6 months, 40% of the work is complete and AC = $54,000. What is the CV? (In dollars, include the sign.)
= -$6,000
? EV = 40% × 120,000 = 48,000. CV = EV − AC = 48,000 − 54,000 = −$6,000 (over budget).

@@
Using the same data (BAC $120,000, 6 of 12 months elapsed, 40% complete, AC $54,000), what is the SPI?
A) 0.80
B) 0.89
C) 1.25
D) 0.40
= A
? PV = 50% × 120,000 = 60,000. SPI = EV / PV = 48,000 / 60,000 = 0.80.

@@
Using the same data, what is the EAC if current cost performance continues?
A) $135,000
B) $126,000
C) $150,000
D) $120,000
= A
? CPI = 48,000 / 54,000 = 0.889. EAC = 120,000 / 0.889 = $135,000.

@@
Using the same data (BAC $120,000, EV $48,000, AC $54,000), what is the TCPI to complete within the BAC?
A) 1.09
B) 0.92
C) 1.00
D) 1.25
= A
? TCPI = (BAC − EV) / (BAC − AC) = 72,000 / 66,000 ≈ 1.09.

@@
Three-point estimates for a task: O = 3 days, M = 6 days, P = 15 days. What are the PERT estimate and standard deviation?
A) 7 days and 2 days
B) 8 days and 2 days
C) 6 days and 3 days
D) 7 days and 1.5 days
= A
? PERT = (3 + 24 + 15) / 6 = 7 days. σ = (15 − 3) / 6 = 2 days.

@@
Two independent sequential activities have PERT standard deviations of 3 days and 4 days. What is the standard deviation of the path?
A) 5 days
B) 7 days
C) 12 days
D) 3.5 days
= A
? Add variances, not standard deviations: 9 + 16 = 25; √25 = 5 days.

@@
A team grows from 5 to 9 people. By how many do the communication channels increase?
A) 26
B) 4
C) 36
D) 10
= A
? 5 people: 10 channels; 9 people: 36 channels; increase = 26.

@@
A risk has a 15% probability and an impact of −$120,000. An opportunity has a 25% probability and an impact of +$40,000. What is the net EMV?
A) −$8,000
B) −$18,000
C) +$10,000
D) −$28,000
= A
? Threat EMV = −18,000; opportunity EMV = +10,000; net = −$8,000.

@@
Option 1: develop in-house for $150,000 with a 20% chance of $50,000 extra cost. Option 2: outsource for $165,000 with a 10% chance of $10,000 extra cost. Which option has the lower expected cost and what is it?
A) Option 1 at $160,000
B) Option 2 at $166,000
C) Option 1 at $150,000
D) Option 2 at $165,000
= A
? Option 1: 150,000 + 0.2 × 50,000 = 160,000. Option 2: 165,000 + 0.1 × 10,000 = 166,000. Option 1 is cheaper.

@@
What is the present value of $133,100 received in 3 years at a 10% discount rate?
A) $100,000
B) $110,000
C) $121,000
D) $93,170
= A
? PV = 133,100 / 1.1³ = 133,100 / 1.331 = $100,000.

@@
An investment of $90,000 yields $20,000 in year 1, $30,000 in year 2 and $40,000 in year 3. What is the simple payback period?
A) 3 years
B) 2 years
C) 2.5 years
D) 4.5 years
= A
? Cumulative inflows: 20,000 after year 1, 50,000 after year 2, 90,000 after year 3. Payback occurs at 3 years.

@@
FPIF contract: target cost $300,000, target profit $30,000, target price $330,000, ceiling price $360,000, buyer/seller share 80/20, actual cost $320,000. What is the final price?
A) $346,000
B) $350,000
C) $360,000
D) $330,000
= A
? Overrun = $20,000; seller absorbs 20% = $4,000; profit = 30,000 − 4,000 = $26,000; price = 320,000 + 26,000 = $346,000, which is below the ceiling.

@@
Using the same FPIF contract (target cost $300,000, target price $330,000, ceiling $360,000, share 80/20), what is the point of total assumption?
A) $337,500
B) $360,000
C) $330,000
D) $345,000
= A
? PTA = (360,000 − 330,000) / 0.8 + 300,000 = 37,500 + 300,000 = $337,500.

@@ | fill
A Kanban system has an average WIP of 18 items and a throughput of 6 items per week. What is the average cycle time in weeks?
= 3
? Little's Law: cycle time = WIP / throughput = 18 / 6 = 3 weeks.

@@
Network: Start → A (5) → C (4) → End; Start → B (3) → D (8) → End; C also depends on B. What is the project duration?
A) 11 days
B) 9 days
C) 12 days
D) 20 days
= A
? Paths: A-C = 5 + 4 = 9; B-D = 3 + 8 = 11; B-C = 3 + 4 = 7 (C starts after the later of A and B, at day 5, finishing at 9). The longest path is B-D at 11 days.
